   "source": [
    "### 1. Verify by hand that this is a valid density, then confirm it numerically with a 2D quadrature."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d09a953a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "*To verify by hand, a valid density must have volume = 1*\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ \\int^1_0 \\int^1_0 (x+y) \\, dxdy $$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ \\int^1_0 \\left[ \\frac{x^2}{2} + y \\right]^1_0 \\, dy = \\int^1_0 (\\frac{1}{2} + y) \\, dy $$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ \\int^1_0 (\\frac{1}{2} + y) \\, dy $$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ \\boxed{ \\left[ \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{y^2}{2} \\right]^1_0 \\,  = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} = 1} $$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 95,
   "id": "b448bade",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Double integral is evaluated to:\t1.0\n",
      "Estimated error:\t\t\t1.663e-14\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Verifying numerically via 2D quadrature\n",
    "\n",
    "from scipy.integrate import dblquad\n",
    "\n",
    "def f_xy(y, x):\n",
    "  return x + y\n",
    "\n",
    "val, err = dblquad(\n",
    "    f_xy,\n",
    "    0,\n",
    "    1,  \n",
    "    lambda x: 0,\n",
    "    lambda x: 1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Double integral is evaluated to:\\t{val}\\n\" + \n",
    "      f\"Estimated error:\\t\\t\\t{err:.3e}\")"
   ]
  },
